## DEC-012: Highlighted Top Status Note Banner & Self-Registering Windows Toast AUMID (`v0.3.1`)
- **Date**: 2026-10-27
- **Context**: Local verification of `v0.3.0` identified three UX and notification refinements:
  1. The legacy bottom checkbox ("Manage reservations & status notes") duplicated the upper-right header navigation button; an explicit instruction pointing users to the upper-right button is cleaner.
  2. Active broadcast Status Notes needed a highlighted banner at the top of the Status View (normal font size) that jumps to `#status-notes` when clicked and can be temporarily closed until the browser page is refreshed (`F5`) or a new note is posted.
  3. On Windows 10/11, `ToastNotificationManager::CreateToastNotifier('PC.Handoff')` silently drops toast notifications (returning exit code `0`) unless `'PC.Handoff'` is registered under `HKCU:\Software\Classes\AppUserModelId\PC.Handoff`.
- **Decision**:
  1. Removed the legacy `showReservationControls` checkbox and replaced it on `StatusView` with an instruction directing users to **⚙️ Manage Queue & Notes** at the upper right.
  2. Added `renderTopStatusNoteBanner` in `status_view.py` rendering the top active `StatusNoteItem` as a highlighted `st.info` banner with an anchor link to `#status-notes` and a temporary `✕` close button (`st.session_state["dismissedTopNoteId"]`).
  3. Updated `buildToastCommand` in `windows_notifier.py` to ensure `HKCU:\Software\Classes\AppUserModelId\PC.Handoff` (`DisplayName = 'PC Handoff'`) exists before calling `CreateToastNotifier`, with automatic fallback to Windows PowerShell's built-in AUMID.

## 2026-10-27 — DEC-013: Dashboard UI/UX Card Redesign, Active User+IP Badge, and Console N/A
- **Context**: Review of the `v0.3.1` dashboard identified visual hierarchy issues (oversizedManage Queue button, fragmented top status and announcement banner, lack of card boundaries between Active Sessions, Reservation Queue, and Status Notes, and stacked vertical forms in `ManageView`), plus two functional clarity needs: displaying the active username and IP directly in the `"In Use"` status banner, and showing `"N/A"` instead of `"Unknown"` for `Client name` and `Client IP` on `Console` sessions.
- **Decision**:
  1. Grouped the top status badge and top Status Note banner inside a cohesive `st.container(border=True)` card, and tightened header navigation proportions to `st.columns([5, 1], vertical_alignment="center")`.
  2. Wrapped Active/Disconnected Sessions, Reservation Queue & Handoff, and Status Notes in separate `st.container(border=True)` cards on `StatusView`, and converted `ManageView` forms into multi-column card layouts using only native Streamlit components (`unsafe_allow_html` remains forbidden).
  3. Updated `badgeTextFor` in `view_model.py` to format `PcStatus.IN_USE` as `"In Use — <user> (<ip>)"` and updated `activeRow` to render `"N/A"` for `clientName` and `clientIp` when `session.connectionType is ConnectionType.CONSOLE` (while preserving `"Unknown"` for RDP sessions with missing client metadata per REQ-001 AC-9).

---

## 2026-10-27 — DEC-014: Interactive Status Buttons, Collapsible Dashboard Cards, and Elastic Spacing (`v0.3.3`)
- **Context**: In `v0.3.2`, the dashboard displayed passive status alerts and cards. For `v0.3.3`, requirements called for:
  1. Status bar navigation: "In Use" and "Next in queue" boxes navigating directly to their respective sections without opening new tabs.
  2. The entire "In Use" and "Next in queue" boxes behaving as clickable buttons rather than text-only markdown links.
  3. Status UI icon indicators: `🔴` prefix for "In Use", `🟢` prefix for "Available".
  4. Collapsible sections: Active sessions, Reservation queue, and Status notes collapsed by default, with `[Expand all]` and `[Collapse all]` controls and user state retention across auto-refreshes.
  5. Elastic spacing: Ensuring `"🕒 Est. wait: Ready now (~0 min)"` comfortably stays on a single line without wrapping.
- **Decision**:
  1. Render the primary "In Use" badge in `StatusView` as a full-width `st.button` (`use_container_width=True`) that expands `Active sessions` on click in the same tab, avoiding browser new-tab behavior triggered by non-anchor markdown links. When "Available", standard `st.success` is rendered with `🟢 Available`.
  2. Render "Next in queue" as a full-width `st.button` when a reservation is queued or ready, expanding the `Reservation queue` section on click, and displaying countdown urgency `(Ready: MM:SS)` when in `READY` state.
  3. Use pure internal in-page fragment anchors (`#active-sessions`, `#reservation-queue`, `#status-notes`) and remove query parameter wrappers that caused Streamlit markdown to inject `target="_blank"`.
  4. Implement `[Expand all]` and `[Collapse all]` control buttons above the collapsible sections, with state persisted in `st.session_state`.
  5. Adjusted top status row column ratios to `[3.2, 3.0, 0.4, 3.4]` in both `StatusView` and `ManageView`, dedicating 34% width to `waitCol` so wait estimates do not line-wrap.
- **Consequences**:
  - Clean dashboard interaction with instant section expansion on click.
  - Zero new tabs opened when clicking status items or banner links.
  - Zero unhandled exceptions or lint violations, with coverage exceeding 99%.

